WEBVTT

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:39.930
Congratulations.

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:42.160
Your application has been approved.

00:01:43.730 --> 00:01:47.100
Funeral will retain possession of the EX-1.

00:01:49.610 --> 00:01:51.000
Thank you, sir.

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:54.990
The outskirts of Montreal...

00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:57.970
...is where I bought a house.

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:02.180
In two more years,

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:08.490
I hope to retire there with
the little lady and our rose bushes.

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:16.960
Don't worry, General.

00:02:18.370 --> 00:02:21.540
You'll get your rose garden and peace of mind.

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:25.910
But don't think I'm doing this just for you.

00:02:47.530 --> 00:02:50.170
I've locked onto the alien's coordinates.

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:51.870
I'll get it before it surfaces.

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:55.300
Dan.

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:56.640
Lt. Simmons.

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:57.710
Yes?

00:02:57.710 --> 00:03:00.910
Angry soldiers are the first to die.

00:03:00.910 --> 00:03:02.580
Understand?

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:03.550
Yes, sir!

00:03:09.990 --> 00:03:11.490
I'm going too.

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:14.420
Watch Dan's back.

00:03:14.990 --> 00:03:16.480
If I'm ordered to.

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:25.850
Once the SARGs are deployed,
take us to 2,200.

00:03:26.770 --> 00:03:27.900
We'll wait at that altitude.

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:29.070
Yes, sir!

00:03:47.420 --> 00:03:49.230
Second Lt. Ryu Soma.

00:03:49.230 --> 00:03:52.790
Unfortunately, it's too early
to get on the stage.

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:56.300
You'll have to watch from the sidelines.

00:04:00.570 --> 00:04:02.510
SARGs 1 and 3 ejected.

00:04:02.510 --> 00:04:04.470
Approaching target.

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:06.840
Lt. Soma?

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:07.810
Ma'am.

00:04:07.810 --> 00:04:09.450
Sit down.

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:10.710
Thank you.

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:25.630
Formation Bravo!

00:04:26.230 --> 00:04:27.200
Roger.

00:04:38.140 --> 00:04:40.010
SARG 1 transformation confirmed.

00:04:40.010 --> 00:04:43.100
SARG 3 transformation also confirmed.

00:05:09.270 --> 00:05:10.800
Don't forget me!

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:18.850
I'm bringing you down!

00:05:53.750 --> 00:05:55.750
Moving just as projected.

00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:58.550
Lame. What's the fun in that?

00:06:27.850 --> 00:06:29.750
Guenevere, between the eyes!

00:06:33.890 --> 00:06:35.860
Initializing firing liquid.

00:06:35.860 --> 00:06:38.310
Ballistic pressure 62.7%.

00:06:46.370 --> 00:06:47.630
Hurry, Guenevere!

00:06:57.080 --> 00:06:58.680
Initialization complete.

00:06:58.680 --> 00:06:59.650
Fire!

00:07:11.590 --> 00:07:13.660
It just evaporated!

00:07:14.150 --> 00:07:16.550
A progressive alien?

00:07:17.530 --> 00:07:19.940
Dan, Guenevere, pull out!

00:07:19.940 --> 00:07:22.100
Analyze that data immediately!

00:07:22.100 --> 00:07:23.150
Y-Yes, ma'am.

00:07:41.990 --> 00:07:42.960
Dan!

00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:52.740
W-What the hell?

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:53.700
Dan!

00:08:02.950 --> 00:08:03.880
Damn.

00:08:19.960 --> 00:08:21.160
Damn it...

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:23.900
Captain! Captain, respond!

00:08:32.940 --> 00:08:34.880
Captain, we need back up!

00:08:34.880 --> 00:08:36.210
Negative! Pull out!

00:08:36.210 --> 00:08:38.880
But we've only just started!

00:08:38.880 --> 00:08:39.850
Roger.

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:43.050
Can't you see that?

00:08:51.560 --> 00:08:55.260
We're not dumb enough to fight
a volcano with a gun, right?

00:09:01.900 --> 00:09:03.910
Progressive alien?

00:09:03.910 --> 00:09:05.810
It assimilates energy...

00:09:05.810 --> 00:09:08.640
...turning our own firepower against us.

00:09:08.640 --> 00:09:10.850
Attack pattern confirmed.

00:09:10.850 --> 00:09:12.510
Using organic magnets,

00:09:12.510 --> 00:09:16.150
it draws in particles like a plasma torch.

00:09:16.150 --> 00:09:18.490
Temperature exceeds 30,000 Kelvin.

00:09:18.490 --> 00:09:23.030
Classification number A56-095.

00:09:23.030 --> 00:09:24.380
It appears to be a Type H2.

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:26.290
Type H2?

00:09:27.330 --> 00:09:29.870
November of 2056.

00:09:29.870 --> 00:09:33.540
The air force spotted one
in the Frankfurt Conflict.

00:09:33.540 --> 00:09:40.940
They tried fire bombing it with
thousands of tons of explosives.

00:09:42.810 --> 00:09:46.880
But that was like giving the H2
the keys to an energy store.

00:09:46.880 --> 00:09:49.920
It started glowing like a small sun,

00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:54.620
and the air force needed
another small sun to stop it.

00:09:54.620 --> 00:09:58.650
It burned 17 villages and 5 cities before then.

00:10:19.050 --> 00:10:20.350
Projected destination?

00:10:23.050 --> 00:10:24.550
Pilgrimage Point.

00:10:25.490 --> 00:10:26.650
It figures.

00:10:29.090 --> 00:10:31.560
You've got to let me go back out there!

00:10:31.560 --> 00:10:33.230
Negative.

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:34.660
There's too much damage.

00:10:34.660 --> 00:10:36.230
There's still SARG 4.

00:10:36.230 --> 00:10:38.480
Hey, that's mine!

00:10:39.470 --> 00:10:43.070
Did you forget the one shot kill rule?

00:10:43.070 --> 00:10:46.840
If you're going to attack a progressive alien...

00:10:46.840 --> 00:10:49.190
...be sure you have enough firepower.

00:10:49.480 --> 00:10:52.450
Unless you want to create another sun.

00:10:53.780 --> 00:10:54.850
Yes.

00:10:54.850 --> 00:10:56.190
Understood.

00:10:56.190 --> 00:11:02.060
They all seem to go there,
though no one knows why.

00:11:04.690 --> 00:11:10.590
But we can't let them keep going,
so there's no turning back.

00:11:12.570 --> 00:11:16.500
If it crosses the yellow zone,
and the candle goes up...

00:11:22.310 --> 00:11:23.970
Don't worry, sir.

00:11:25.680 --> 00:11:27.650
We'll use "it."

00:11:27.650 --> 00:11:29.180
Will it work?

00:11:29.180 --> 00:11:30.250
I think so.

00:11:32.820 --> 00:11:36.730
Just do it before it hits the yellow zone.

00:11:36.730 --> 00:11:38.730
And dump all records...

00:11:38.730 --> 00:11:40.090
I understand.

00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:47.340
But...

00:11:47.340 --> 00:11:49.030
...will it really work?

00:11:53.210 --> 00:11:55.110
Get me the 22nd floor.

00:11:55.110 --> 00:11:58.710
Tell the teacher to send Harriet Bartholomew.

00:11:59.750 --> 00:12:01.320
To the control deck?

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:03.420
That's right.

00:12:03.420 --> 00:12:04.390
Lt. Soma...

00:12:04.390 --> 00:12:08.160
...be prepared for my orders in SARG 5.

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:09.520
Understood.

00:12:13.560 --> 00:12:15.410
I don't like these odds.

00:12:28.840 --> 00:12:31.350
Commander, it's from the 22nd floor.

00:12:31.350 --> 00:12:34.050
They can't find Harriet Bartholomew.

00:12:41.890 --> 00:12:44.530
Commander, we've located her.

00:12:44.530 --> 00:12:46.220
She's in SARG 5's cockpit.

00:12:47.450 --> 00:12:48.450
What?

00:12:53.770 --> 00:12:55.640
What are you doing, Lt. Soma?

00:12:55.640 --> 00:12:57.100
Why is Harriet there?

00:12:58.140 --> 00:12:59.590
Early parole.

00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:02.670
We need her for the EX-1.

00:13:07.150 --> 00:13:08.800
What now, Commander?

00:13:10.020 --> 00:13:10.990
Commander?

00:13:13.590 --> 00:13:15.960
Release all locks immediately.

00:13:15.960 --> 00:13:17.720
Open all emergency hatches.

00:13:19.090 --> 00:13:22.130
I repeat. Do as Lt. Soma asks.

00:13:22.130 --> 00:13:24.000
Get the EX-1 ready!

00:13:59.500 --> 00:14:00.900
Mr. Fairy!

00:14:01.140 --> 00:14:02.590
Mr. Fairy!

00:14:12.180 --> 00:14:13.630
Mr. Fairy!

00:14:27.700 --> 00:14:31.600
Control tower reports SARG 5
and the EX-1 are airborne.

00:14:40.180 --> 00:14:42.740
Hey, I can't see Mr. Fairy.

00:14:42.740 --> 00:14:44.150
What happened?

00:14:44.150 --> 00:14:45.250
Oh, there he is!

00:14:53.120 --> 00:14:56.060
Look at him go! He's so handsome.

00:14:56.060 --> 00:15:00.430
Hey, these clothes are all hot and baggy.

00:15:00.430 --> 00:15:04.030
Hey, do you know where
the real land of the fairies is?

00:15:04.030 --> 00:15:05.180
Is it far from here?

00:15:05.990 --> 00:15:09.680
Do you think Walton's okay all by himself?

00:15:29.890 --> 00:15:30.860
Captain!

00:15:30.860 --> 00:15:32.860
What's taking the commander so long?

00:15:32.860 --> 00:15:33.860
Calm down.

00:15:33.860 --> 00:15:34.960
But...

00:15:35.630 --> 00:15:37.570
Something's approaching on the scanner.

00:15:37.570 --> 00:15:39.500
Is it the air force?

00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:40.650
Check the IFF.

00:15:40.650 --> 00:15:41.500
Yes, sir.

00:15:44.370 --> 00:15:46.980
SARG 5 and the EX-1?

00:15:46.980 --> 00:15:48.740
Second Lt. Soma.

00:15:48.740 --> 00:15:51.650
Lt. Soma, you're flying too low!

00:15:51.650 --> 00:15:53.350
You're not ready yet.

00:15:53.350 --> 00:15:55.100
I won't be fighting.

00:15:56.720 --> 00:15:59.090
I need to borrow the EX-1.

00:15:59.090 --> 00:16:01.670
We're not at the land of the fairies yet?

00:16:01.670 --> 00:16:03.890
What? Hattie's there too?

00:16:03.890 --> 00:16:05.420
What's he doing?

00:16:08.630 --> 00:16:10.330
How much further?

00:16:10.330 --> 00:16:11.930
Are we almost there?

00:16:11.930 --> 00:16:13.870
Mr. Fairy must be tired.

00:16:13.870 --> 00:16:14.840
Shut up.

00:16:24.610 --> 00:16:27.080
What's that civilian doing there?

00:16:27.080 --> 00:16:28.580
It's a war zone.

00:16:28.580 --> 00:16:29.950
No choice.

00:16:29.950 --> 00:16:32.590
This is to keep Funeral's flag waving.

00:16:32.590 --> 00:16:35.420
Have you thought about Harriet?

00:16:35.420 --> 00:16:36.350
Of course.

00:16:36.350 --> 00:16:37.950
SARG 5 is closing in!

00:16:50.610 --> 00:16:52.850
Kill each other, you monsters!

00:17:03.190 --> 00:17:04.400
Mr. Fairy!

00:17:18.870 --> 00:17:20.800
Stop! Let go of Mr. Fairy!

00:17:20.800 --> 00:17:23.040
That's not a fairy.

00:17:23.040 --> 00:17:25.070
It's not even alive.

00:17:25.070 --> 00:17:26.440
It's just a machine.

00:17:26.440 --> 00:17:28.670
No, it's an iron monster!

00:17:29.880 --> 00:17:31.410
He's not a monster!

00:17:31.410 --> 00:17:34.280
He's a fairy!

00:17:34.280 --> 00:17:37.200
Whenever I'm in trouble,
he comes to help me!

00:17:37.600 --> 00:17:39.400
Then sing.

00:17:40.700 --> 00:17:41.920
Do it.

00:17:41.920 --> 00:17:42.910
For him.

00:18:12.520 --> 00:18:13.900
Mr. Fairy!

00:18:17.690 --> 00:18:18.640
You can do it!

00:18:18.830 --> 00:18:19.900
You can do it!

00:18:27.970 --> 00:18:36.340
<i>They say they saw it in the shadow.</i>

00:18:36.340 --> 00:18:40.880
<i>Little cricket.</i>

00:18:40.880 --> 00:18:47.420
<i>It jumps and plays on the green grass.</i>

00:18:47.420 --> 00:18:55.760
<i>The children laugh and they all dance with the little cricket.</i>

00:18:55.760 --> 00:18:58.130
<i>Glistening in the light.</i>

00:19:09.540 --> 00:19:11.380
The EX-1 is winning!

00:19:11.380 --> 00:19:12.950
No, it's not good.

00:19:12.950 --> 00:19:14.420
Too many blows.

00:19:14.420 --> 00:19:17.040
That friction's going to turn into heat.

00:19:31.930 --> 00:19:36.270
<i>In the windy, deep night...</i>

00:19:36.270 --> 00:19:39.570
<i>I saw a light,</i>

00:19:39.570 --> 00:19:45.680
<i>which I have seen before in all my dreams.</i>

00:19:45.680 --> 00:19:52.280
<i>The stars will guide me, then we'll be free.</i>

00:20:51.580 --> 00:20:53.150
Mr. Fairy!

00:20:53.150 --> 00:20:55.450
Mr. Fairy, are you okay?

00:21:04.560 --> 00:21:06.630
I'm okay, too.

00:21:06.630 --> 00:21:09.300
I'm fine, see?

00:21:09.300 --> 00:21:11.050
So don't be mad.

00:21:13.970 --> 00:21:15.230
See? See?

00:21:17.570 --> 00:21:20.270
Your hand is so warm!

00:21:22.640 --> 00:21:25.590
You're the only good fairy.

00:21:27.580 --> 00:21:28.930
You're wrong.

00:21:30.100 --> 00:21:32.250
He's not a monster.

00:21:32.250 --> 00:21:33.320
You're a liar!

00:21:33.320 --> 00:21:35.020
You're a liar, and you're bad!

00:21:37.090 --> 00:21:38.120
Liar.

00:21:50.070 --> 00:21:52.510
Reports sent to all relevant ministries.

00:21:52.510 --> 00:21:55.450
Defense level downgraded from red to yellow.

00:21:55.980 --> 00:21:56.990
Well done.

00:21:59.010 --> 00:22:01.450
Captain Hartland on the line.

00:22:01.450 --> 00:22:02.640
Patch him through.

00:22:04.590 --> 00:22:05.750
Commander.

00:22:05.750 --> 00:22:09.160
I don't approve of today's operation.

00:22:09.160 --> 00:22:11.930
The involvement of a civilian,

00:22:11.930 --> 00:22:13.730
and the omission from the-

00:22:13.730 --> 00:22:15.250
I'm a heartless witch.

00:22:19.970 --> 00:22:24.720
Mettle and valor are words we reserve for men.

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:34.910
Hatred and War

00:22:36.220 --> 00:22:38.070
Burning memories.

00:22:38.850 --> 00:22:41.890
On the horizon day after day.

00:22:41.890 --> 00:22:44.980
A bush of thorns around a white ribbon.

00:22:46.060 --> 00:22:48.760
Next time,
War and Escape.
